<div class="centered-article-text">
  <p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 20px; max-width: 500px; margin: 20px auto;">
 	Originally launched in 2017, the Alpine Jacket was Adsum’s foray into down fill outerwear alongside the Alpine Vest. Down is similar to the wool pieces we touched on in last week’s post, as it also comes from a natural source. It can arguably be considered the single best insulator available for use in warm weather clothing.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 20px; max-width: 500px; margin: 20px auto;">
     We changed the exterior shell fabric of the FW20 Alpine Jacket to a soft touch, water resistant ripstop 100% nylon ripstop taffeta. Jacket details and fit remain the same from FW19 including integrated stretch ponte storm cuffs, a interior storm placket to stop any draft coming through the center front YKK vislon zipper teeth, metal snap closure patch pockets, a cinchable high throat hood and zippered interior stow pocket.
  </p>
